  "title": "Native creation keeps each Fano atom whole and reads each cut's direction",
  "subject": "What native creation sees inside a Fano atom and across a cut between two atoms",
  "conclusion": "A Fano atom's lines create at one another in both directions, as in the complete Fano plane (proved for atoms attached at a line by the screening lemma, computed for atoms attached at a point). Across a cut between two atoms, the receiver's cut lines and the emitter's lines are mutual while its intact lines create one way at the emitter's (676 of 676 pairs), and lines sharing two points are silent.",
